<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIA-TELECOMS-Details of Telstra sale bill.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIA-TELECOMS-Details of Telstra sale bill.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian government's bill for the partial sale of telecoms carrier Telstra Corp is expected to come up for debate in the Senate around October 28, according to government sources.</p>
<p>However, the bills faces strong opposition and its passage depends on two independent senators, Brian Harradine and Mal Colston, as the government does not have a majority in the Senate.</p>
<p>The Labor opposition and minor parties have pledged to block the sale, but Harradine and Colston have not yet declared their position.</p>
</text>
